.TH BLUETOOTH-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "bluetooth-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bluetooth-revamped \- connected Bluetooth devices and their battery in tmux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluetooth-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B status
.I name
.br
.B bluetooth-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B bluetooth-revamped refresh
.br
.B bluetooth-revamped doctor
.br
.B bluetooth-revamped version
.br
.B bluetooth-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bluetooth-revamped
shows every connected Bluetooth device and its battery in the tmux status
line. The entry point
.B bluetooth-revamped.tmux
replaces the placeholders
.BR #{bluetooth} ,
.BR #{bluetooth_icon} ,
.B #{bluetooth_count}
and
.B #{bluetooth_min}
in
.B status-left
and
.B status-right
with calls to
.BR "bluetooth-revamped status" .
Each call prints the reading stored in a tmux option at once, and starts one
background reading when the stored one is older than the interval.
.PP
macOS reads
.BR "system_profiler SPBluetoothDataType" ;
Linux reads
.BR "upower \-\-dump" .
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI status " name"
Print one placeholder:
.B device
for every device and its battery,
.B icon
for the icon while a device is connected,
.B count
for the number of devices, or
.B min
for the device with the lowest battery.
.TP
.B list
Read the devices now, store the reading and print one device per line.
.TP
.B refresh
Read the devices now and store the reading for the status line.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the Bluetooth reader, gum, the desktop
notifier and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " seconds"
How long a reading stays fresh. The default is 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " format"
The printf format for the device list. The default is
.BR %s .
.TP
.BI \-\-separator " text"
The text between devices. The default is a comma and a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon " text"
The text for the icon placeholder. The default is
.BR BT .
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
Each option also takes the form
.IR \-\-name = value ,
and
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_INTERVAL ", " BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_FORMAT ", " BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_SEPARATOR ", " BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_ICON
The same as the option of the same name. An option wins over the environment,
and the environment over the tmux option.
.TP
.B BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B BLUETOOTH_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
.TP
.B @bluetooth_revamped_interval
Seconds a reading stays fresh. A value that is not a number means 30.
.TP
.B @bluetooth_revamped_format
The printf format for
.BR #{bluetooth} .
The default is
.BR %s .
.TP
.B @bluetooth_revamped_separator
The text between devices in
.BR #{bluetooth} .
The default is a comma and a space.
.TP
.B @bluetooth_revamped_icon
The text for
.BR #{bluetooth_icon} .
The default is
.BR BT .
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR system_profiler (8),
.BR upower (1)
